Subject: Unset active textures on program relink

While this didn't manifest as a bug, for uniformity with binding a new
program, unsetActiveTextures() is now called when relinking the program
too.  Both operations install a new executable, so it makes sense they
do the same state clean up.

Bug: chromium:536659904
Change-Id: I19c0bd129e03859d242cb15c7e11969385156f2b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/angle/angle/+/8135183
Reviewed-by: Geoff Lang <geofflang@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Shahbaz Youssefi <syoussefi@chromium.org>

